==Icelandic==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|non|is}} {{term|búa|lang=non}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|is}} {{term/t|gem-pro|*būaną}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈpuːa/|lang=is}}
*: {{rhymes|uːa|lang=is}}

===Verb===
{{is-verb-strong|bjó|bjuggu|búið}}

# {{context|intransitive|lang=is}} to [[reside]], to [[live]]{{jump|is|live|s}}
#: ''Ég '''bý''' í Þýskalandi.''
#:: I '''live''' in Germany.
#: ''Þar sem ég '''bý'''.''
#:: In my '''neck of the woods'''.
# {{context|intransitive|lang=is}} to [[run]] a [[farm]] or [[home]]{{jump|is|farm|s}}
#: ''Hann er hættur að '''búa'''.''
#:: He has given up '''farming'''.
# {{context|transitive|governs the accusative|lang=is}} to [[prepare]]{{jump|is|prepare|s}}
# {{context|impersonal|lang=is}} used in set phrases
#: ''Honum '''býr''' eitthvað í brjósti.''
#:: There is something on his mind.

